30,2,,status,Benjamin,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
31,2,,status,Jonathan,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
32,2,,status,Servas,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
33,2,,status,Takumi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
34,2,,status,Asuka,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"My findings are concerning. The late-turn pool is exhausted, and our general crew establishment is severely understaffed. Any plan requiring more driver hours is impossible.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Takumi,,"The data is clear: the ""crowding"" people complain about isn't the real problem. The real time-sink is the connection waiting. We're fixing the wrong things.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,How delightful. It seems we are broke in the areas that matter and paying a premium for ticketing software that likely doesn't work.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Servas,,I found that we have succeeded before. Our past pilots on contactless payments and evening schedules worked well. We need not fear the new if it mirrors the successful old.,"{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"I've found that the ""pre-war shells"" are a black hole for time and money. Furthermore, the joint operators' committee is a bureaucratic maze for certain modes.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Takumi, if the problem is connection waiting, we might need more frequent short-turns. But as I said, the rosters cannot support more shifts.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Takumi,,"Then we change the schedule, not the staff. We need a plan that optimizes the flow of the journey, not one that just adds more trains to a crowded line.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Asuka, @Takumi, please. If we optimize the flow but the funding comes from the operating subsidy—which I've seen is trimmed—we'll be bankrupt by year three.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Asuka"",""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Servas,,"Let us not let fear stifle us. The accessibility programme showed that while some things failed, the core infrastructure rebuilds were successful. We can build if we are focused.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Servas, the ""core rebuilds"" you mention are exactly where the risk lies. The pre-war shells are hiding voids that stop work for weeks. We cannot trust the delivery dates.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Asuka,,I cannot support any plan that increases the burden on the late-turn pool. We are at a breaking point. We need a plan that reduces operational stress.,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Takumi,,"I don't care about the ""stress"" of the system if the passengers are wasting twenty minutes waiting for a transfer. We need to prioritize the total journey time.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"I am looking for a plan that utilizes the ring-fenced construction balance. If we can use capital grants rather than operating funds, we might actually survive.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Servas,,"It is a beautiful thing to see you all so passionate. But remember, the contactless trial worked because it was simple. Let us choose the plan that is most elegant in its simplicity.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"Simplicity is a virtue, but transparency is better. Any plan that involves heavy work in the old shells or requires joint operator consensus is a high-risk gamble.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
